---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getAppConfig, SITE_URL } from "../../lib/catalog";

const appConfig = await getAppConfig();
const pageUrl = `${SITE_URL}/guides/allahs-right-over-his-servants/`;
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: "What Is Allah’s Right Upon His Servants?",
      description:
        "A reading guide to the opening chapter of Kitab at-Tawheed: its focus on worship, Tawheed, and studying the original text with an explanation.",
      mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
      inLanguage: "en",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Al Marfa Duroos" },
      about: {
        "@type": "Book",
        name: "Kitab at-Tawheed",
        alternateName: "كتاب التوحيد الذي هو حق الله على العبيد",
        author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab" },
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE_URL },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Kitab at-Tawheed", item: `${SITE_URL}/kitab-al-tawheed/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Allah’s Right Upon His Servants", item: pageUrl },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="What Is Allah’s Right Upon His Servants? | Kitab at-Tawheed Guide"
  description="Read a source-based guide to the opening chapter of Kitab at-Tawheed: worship, Tawheed, and how to study the original Arabic text with the Urdu explanation."
  {appConfig}
  ogType="article"
  articleTags={["Kitab at-Tawheed", "Tawheed", "Islamic creed", "Islamic study"]}
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} slot="head" />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-10 min-w-0" data-pagefind-body>
    <nav class="text-xs text-fg-3 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#C9A84C]">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-1">→</span>
      <a href="/kitab-al-tawheed/" class="hover:text-[#C9A84C]">Kitab at-Tawheed</a>
      <span class="mx-1">→</span>
      <span class="text-fg-2">Allah’s Right Upon His Servants</span>
    </nav>

    <p class="text-[#C9A84C] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Opening chapter reading guide</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-balance">What Is Allah’s Right Upon His Servants?</h1>
    <p class="text-[#C9A84C] text-lg mb-6" lang="ar" dir="rtl">كتاب التوحيد الذي هو حق الله على العبيد</p>

    <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      The opening chapter of <strong class="text-fg">Kitab at-Tawheed</strong>
      frames the book around a central question: what is due to Allah from His
      servants? In the chapter’s wording and collected evidences, the answer is
      connected to worshipping Allah alone. This is why the opening is a useful
      place to begin before moving into the later, more specific chapters.
    </p>
    <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      This page is a reading guide, not an independent religious ruling or a
      replacement for the text and its explanation. Read the cited source text,
      listen to the lesson in sequence, and take questions to a qualified teacher.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">What the opening chapter brings together</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-fg">Worship and Tawheed.</strong> The chapter treats
          worship of Allah alone as the practical meaning of Tawheed, rather than
          as an abstract term to memorise.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-fg">The message of the prophets.</strong> Its
          evidences connect this call to the mission of the prophets, giving the
          reader a framework for why the subject is foundational in the book.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-fg">Rights and responsibility.</strong> The chapter
          asks the reader to consider worship as a duty owed to Allah, then points
          to the texts that explain this duty and its place in a believer’s life.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-surface border border-[var(--divider)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Read the source text alongside this guide</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The best way to use a reading guide is to keep the source open. The site
        provides the opening chapter in its original Arabic and in the bilingual
        Urdu reading edition, including the chapter’s own summary points.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
        <a href="/arabic/book/ch-00/" class="text-center bg-[#C9A84C] text-black font-bold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-sm hover:bg-[#D4B55C]">Read the Arabic text</a>
        <a href="/urdu/book/ch-00/" class="text-center border border-[#C9A84C]/50 text-[#C9A84C] font-bold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-sm hover:bg-[#C9A84C]/10">Read with Urdu translation</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Questions to carry into your study</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
        <li>How does the chapter connect Tawheed with worship?</li>
        <li>Which evidences does it place at the beginning, and what does each add to the topic?</li>
        <li>How does the chapter describe the shared call of the prophets?</li>
        <li>Which point from the chapter’s summary needs further explanation from a teacher?</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-[var(--divider)] pt-7">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Continue studying</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/study-notes/class-01-part-01/" class="block bg-surface border border-[var(--divider)] rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-[#C9A84C]/40 transition-colors">
          <p class="text-xs text-fg-3 mb-1">Urdu audio companion</p>
          <p class="font-semibold">Start with Class 01, Part 01 <span class="text-[#C9A84C]">→</span></p>
        </a>
        <a href="/kitab-al-tawheed/" class="block bg-surface border border-[var(--divider)] rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-[#C9A84C]/40 transition-colors">
          <p class="text-xs text-fg-3 mb-1">Series overview</p>
          <p class="font-semibold">What is Kitab at-Tawheed? <span class="text-[#C9A84C]">→</span></p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
